{
    "about": "The root names of the site (documentation/Canonical Form.md, section \"The root names of the site\"). Both implementations read every case: `reserved` gives a name and whether it is a reserved root name, `folded` gives two texts and whether they have one folded form, `obsidian` gives a vault path and the path that Obsidian gives it (its `normalizePath`, section \"Paths\"), `twins` gives paths and, for each path whose Obsidian path is the Obsidian path of another one, the first such other path in the order of the code points. `windows` gives a vault path and whether Windows cannot hold it (section \"Paths\", rule 5, decision R82). `windowsNames` gives one name of a file or a folder and whether Windows opens another entry for it (a dot or a space at the end, or a reserved name of a device): the vault holds no entry with such a name (section \"The notes of the vault\", rule 5, issue 79).",
